                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "From my hours count you can see how I actually love this game (and I bought 12 and 13 versions...).\n\nAnd this is really sad for me to say this: DON'T BUY THIS GAME.\n\nOr don't buy it again...\n\nThe problem isn't if this is the best cycling simulation game (for what it's worth, it's also the only...), but if this game is worth is price.\n\nThe answer is NO.\n\nFor the last 4 years the game is remaneid actually pretty the same: some new graphic, some new features and some solved bugs.\n\nAnd today?\n- The new features are often broken or bugged, you often have to buy the NEW YEAR version to have them working, because the patches are often very modest and don't change much of the gameplay.\n- The sim engine (3D race and fast sim, there was only a most advanced fast sim, and this was so bugged they decided to remove it rather than improve it...) hasn't changed a lot, quality talking. Same bug, and some modest new features.\n- The game engine is the ALWAYS THE SAME, and have the same bugs.\n\nBugs? During season preparation, I usually go forward and save every 2 or 3 minutes, because, the game crash.\nHow often it crash?\nDuring a season?\nFrom 20 to 40 times.\n\nI'm not kidding, and I'm talking of TOTAL CRASHES.\n\nThis is frankly unacceptable, in my opinion.\nAnd all the three last games of this series crashes for the same bugs.\nThey've never be addressed.\n\nNow, as I said, I really like this game, I will continue to play it, but no, I WILL NOT BUY THE NEXT YEAR VERSION.\n\nBecause it's pointless, I don't pay 4 times a bunch of euros (many, because this is sold like a AAA game) for have ALWAYS THE SAME STUPID PROBLEMS AND NOTHING NEW.\n\nBe aware...",
